FL,305,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30402
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F304A1786411079
OL,3,CSales of cool clothes and garden
OL,4,Caccessories soar as heat dominates
OL,5,Cspending
OL,7,FEngland's progress to the semi-finals
OL,8,Fof the World Cup helped drive a 3.8%
OL,9,Fincrease in food sales, above the 12-
OL,10,Fmonth average of 3.4%.
OL,12,FHowever, non-food sales were down 0.7%
OL,13,Fon last July as shoppers avoided the
OL,14,Fheat of the high street.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G2/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,305,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30403
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F304A1786411079
OL,3,CSales of cool clothes and garden
OL,4,Caccessories soar as heat dominates
OL,5,Cspending
OL,7,FClothing was a bright spot, driven by
OL,8,Fdemand for affordable summer
OL,9,Fessentials, while shoppers also
OL,10,Fprioritised smaller indulgences such
OL,11,Fas beauty products and fashion
OL,12,Fjewellery but delayed bigger-ticket
OL,13,Fpurchases including furniture and
OL,14,Fcomputing.
OL,16,FBRC chief executive Helen Dickinson
OL,17,Fsaid: "Consumer demand has struggled
OL,18,Fin the heat, leaving retailers facing
OL,19,Fa challenging start to the second half
OL,20,Fof the year.
OL,26,@yD@GOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,305,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30404
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F304A1786411079
OL,3,CSales of cool clothes and garden
OL,4,Caccessories soar as heat dominates
OL,5,Cspending
OL,7,F"Household budgets remain stretched,
OL,8,Fconsumer confidence is fragile, and
OL,9,Fretailers continue to grapple with
OL,10,Frising operating costs."
OL,12,FLinda Ellett, UK head of consumer,
OL,13,Fretail and leisure markets at KPMG,
OL,14,Fsaid: "Despite the summer season
OL,15,Fgetting started as early as May, the
OL,16,Fupturn for clothes, shoes and
OL,17,Faccessories has continued right
OL,18,Fthrough to August.
OL,26,@oD@AOUrD@XO]vD@GOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G4/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,305,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30405
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F304A1786411079
OL,3,CSales of cool clothes and garden
OL,4,Caccessories soar as heat dominates
OL,5,Cspending
OL,7,F"The prolonged warm weather has also
OL,8,Faided home entertaining and garden-
OL,9,Frelated purchases and, coupled with
OL,10,FEngland's progress to the tail-end of
OL,11,Fthe World Cup, brought a boost to food
OL,12,Fand drink sales in July."
OL,14,FSeparate figures from Barclays show
OL,15,Fconsumer card spending grew by 2% year
OL,16,Fon year in July, up from 1.9% in June,
OL,17,Fwith England's run at the World Cup,
OL,18,Fthe July heatwave and recovering
OL,19,Fconsumer confidence all contributing
OL,20,Fto the uplift.
OL,26,@oD@AOUtD@YO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G5/8
